<title>UK: Railtrack appoints safety director to board.</title>
<headline>Railtrack appoints safety director to board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Railtrack Plc, the rail infrastructure operator, plans to appoint a new safety and standards director, it said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The appointment of the person responsible for safety  to the group board &quot;confirms Railtrack's commitment to safety&quot; said Railtrack chairman, Sir Robert Horton.</p>
<p>Rod Muttram, currently director of electrical engineering and control systems, will take over safety operations from David Rayner who is to retire at the end of the year.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 5427717.</p>
